      "raw": "<p>That ruling confuses me. &nbsp;What causes the destruction then? &nbsp;It just is destroyed by &quot;the rules?&quot;</p><p>If being at 0hp is a destruction effect independant of the damage that put you at 0hp, then wouldn&#39;t any target destroyed by Haka&#39;s damage not go under Savage Mana? &nbsp;All Haka did was reduce it to 0 or fewer HP, he didn&#39;t destroy it, the rules destroyed it.</p><p>Or is it a matter of missed timing, if the damage causes a target to drop to 0hp and it is destroyed then it counts as destroyed by that damage, but if that immediate destruction is cancelled then the destruction is unrelated to the damage?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Like if Kismet&#39;s last point of health was taken by the Final Wasteland with that one card in play, but Kismet&#39;s lucky card thing prevented her from being destroyed with the first check, but the second card was a lucky card so she was destroyed she would not leave play but just be incapped.</p>",
